    <string name="a11y_lost_title">Home button takeover is off</string>
    <string name="a11y_lost_notes">Android switches this off whenever the app is updated. Turn “Home key to top” back on so the Home button returns to this desk.</string>
    <string name="a11y_lost_go">Turn it on</string>
    <string name="a11y_first_title">Make Home come back here</string>
    <string name="a11y_first_notes">Turn on “Home key to top” in Accessibility, and allow Usage access for this app, so the remote’s Home button returns to this desk.</string>
    <string name="a11y_guide_title">Turn Home takeover on over ADB</string>
    <string name="a11y_guide_notes">This TV has no Accessibility page — the vendor removed it. The switch can only be set from a computer, once.\nTake a photo of this screen, then follow the steps below.\n\n1. Turn on ADB debugging on the TV first. Where it lives varies; usually Settings → General / About this TV. Skyworth/Coocaa hide it in the factory menu: Settings → General → About this TV → TV information → More information, then press Up Up Down Down Left Right Left Right.\n2. On a computer on the same network:\nadb connect YOUR_TV_IP:5555\nadb shell settings put secure enabled_accessibility_services %1$s/com.gathin.tvhome.HomeKeyService\nadb shell settings put secure accessibility_enabled 1\nadb shell appops set %1$s GET_USAGE_STATS allow\n\nEvery app update turns it off again; re-run the two settings commands after updating.</string>
